<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Princess Jincheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 739</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Jincheng of Tang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Princess Jincheng was a Tang princess, an adopted daughter of the emperor Zhongzong, who was sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> in 710 to marry the young emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/me-agtsom">Me Agtsom</a> as part of a peace settlement. The Tang ceded the Jiuqu district on the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> as part of the arrangement. She lived in Tibet until her death in 739 and is remembered as a patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a>.</p></div>
